{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533935-vda20-daimoinon-6-power-hell-born-i\u0307nvestiture","id":1533935,"title":"VDA20 Daimoinon 6 power Hell-born \u0130nvestiture","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-09T22:24:19-07:00","id":1533935,"title":"VDA20 Daimoinon 6 power Hell-born \u0130nvestiture","content":"Hello there,<br /> <br /> Question about the Hell-born \u0130nvestiture power: my reading of it is that it stems from the Baali's own blood and not from a pact to become subservient to a demon. Does anyone read it as a pact? My ST does and therefore he vetoed my idea for a Baali PG with this power, unless \u0130 accepted to have a pact, and \u0130 would have to roleplay its acquisition in game anyway by searching and contacting the demon rather than starting with it through freebie points.<br /> <br /> \u0130t's not a big deal, \u0130 made another character instead, but \u0130 really don't see why he thinks this power should entail a pact, especially since there is already a Merit for that in the Tome of Secrets, other than an issue of bad translation in \u0130talian where they translated &quot;investiture&quot; with &quot;patto (pact)&quot; rather than &quot;investitura (investiture)&quot;.<br /> <br /> Am \u0130 alone in how \u0130 read this power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T01:20:28-07:00","id":1533942,"title":"","content":"The name Investiture and the description that it comes from the blood of the Baali strongly suggest that it is not a pact, but that the vampire themselves is becoming more demonical. Contrast that with the modern V20 Daimonion level 6 power (Concordance) where it is explicitly a pact with a cost. DA Baali see themselves at least equal to demons if not superior, while modern Baali have switched roles.<br /> <br /> If you go by older edition material, demonic <i>investments </i>(not investitures) are something even <i>mortals </i>can make, so it seems silly to me that you would need a level 6 Discipline power - multiple times! - to achieve the same effect. So yeah, it's a poor translation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T03:25:28-07:00","id":1533948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533935-vda20-daimoinon-6-power-hell-born-i\u0307nvestiture?p=1533942#post1533942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The name Investiture and the description that it comes from the blood of the Baali strongly suggest that it is not a pact, but that the vampire themselves is becoming more demonical. Contrast that with the modern V20 Daimonion level 6 power (Concordance) where it is explicitly a pact with a cost. DA Baali see themselves at least equal to demons if not superior, while modern Baali have switched roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly: especially the Molochim (what my character should have been) don't make deals, they just try to take little amounts of power from the diluted True Names of the Children - ensuring it's not so much that it would stir them from their sleep. And Daimoinon in VDA20 can be used against demons, too, so it's pretty clear that not every Baali has to be subservient to demons to access the full powers of this discipline. It's also pointless since there is a merit for 5 or 6 points, as I said, that gives you just that: a super power (including the chance to have children despite being a vampire) in exchange for a pact with a demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T23:55:49-07:00","id":1535705,"title":"","content":"I actually want to expand on this a bit because I always wondered this. If some Baali decides to follow Zettler's or Petaniqua's example and pledge infernal fealty to the Wyrm, does that mean they're geting Fomori powers or BSD gfits as Hell-born investiture/concordance or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T01:20:22-07:00","id":1535707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533935-vda20-daimoinon-6-power-hell-born-i\u0307nvestiture?p=1535705#post1535705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually want to expand on this a bit because I always wondered this. If some Baali decides to follow Zettler's or Petaniqua's example and pledge infernal fealty to the Wyrm, does that mean they're geting Fomori powers or BSD gfits as Hell-born investiture/concordance or what?</div> </div> </div> </div>No Gifts (unless they somehow have a Gnosis score), but Fomor powers are not only possible but likely. Technically it wouldn't exactly be an infernal pact, although I think for simplicity in non-crossover chronicles it is categorized as such. There are rules in either <i>WTA:Possessed </i>or<i> Freak Legion </i>for what happens if a Bane possesses a vampire, I can't check atm. But a spirit pact has similar results.<br /> <br /> There is also a Dark Thaumaturgy Path (Die Herrschaft des Wyrm) that specifcally deals with Wyrm stuff in a VtM context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T12:06:17-07:00","id":1535743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533935-vda20-daimoinon-6-power-hell-born-i\u0307nvestiture?p=1535707#post1535707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No Gifts (unless they somehow have a Gnosis score), but Fomor powers are not only possible but likely. Technically it wouldn't exactly be an infernal pact, although I think for simplicity in non-crossover chronicles it is categorized as such. There are rules in either <i>WTA:Possessed </i>or<i> Freak Legion </i>for what happens if a Bane possesses a vampire, I can't check atm. But a spirit pact has similar results.<br /> <br /> There is also a Dark Thaumaturgy Path (Die Herrschaft des Wyrm) that specifcally deals with Wyrm stuff in a VtM context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ngl, you could built some pretty busted vamps using Fomori powers. And not just with the usual sibjects like Spirit Ties, Molecular Weakening, Homogeneity and Mega-Attributes. Imagine having a vampire with Immunity: Sunlight.<br /> <br /> And yes, you're correct, there are two types of banes known to possess kindred. Blood Thirsters and Rot Walkers.<br /> <br /> The first turns them into mindless -but strong- monsters called 'Bloodworms' that are pretty much the vampires from <i>The Strain</i>. The second, on the other hand, not only lets them keeps their sapience but gives them massive power boosts in the form of resistance to sunlight (inflicts only bashing damage), the ability to stay awake for most of the day and being able to turn people into zombie thralls with their bite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T05:51:07-07:00","id":1535766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533935-vda20-daimoinon-6-power-hell-born-i\u0307nvestiture?p=1535743#post1535743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ngl, you could built some pretty busted vamps using Fomori powers. And not just with the usual sibjects like Spirit Ties, Molecular Weakening, Homogeneity and Mega-Attributes. Imagine having a vampire with Immunity: Sunlight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, paying the cost of a level 6 Clan Discipline for each isn't cheap. For that cost, most Fomor powers are overpriced. They also can't cancel out Cain's curse (VDA20 makes this explicit), so things like Immunity:Sunlight are out. As ST, I also would keep the deformities that come with them as additional price to pay and treat them as part of the vampire's body stasis like the Nosferatu curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T07:01:22-07:00","id":1535769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533935-vda20-daimoinon-6-power-hell-born-i\u0307nvestiture?p=1535766#post1535766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They also can't cancel out Cain's curse (VDA20 makes this explicit), so things like Immunity:Sunlight are out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. Daimoinon 6 can't cancel, specifically, the need for blood, vulnerability to sunlight and vulnerability to True Faith, but it can and does cancel vulnerability to fire.<br /> <br /> The Corpse in the Monster path of Necromancy makes you more or less immune to sunlight and fire and able to function by day as long as you can spend 12 blood points per night and don't mind higher difficulties for frenzy (but one of the options for Daimoinon 6 frees you from the need for a Road and frenzy checks, so let me add a Cappadocian Baali to my to-do list).<br /> <br /> The Merit from VDA20 Tome of Secrets Demonic Patron (\u0130 think this is the name, \u0130 might be remembering the name wrong) for 6 freebies allows you to overturn aspects of Cain's curse giving the ability to eat meat if it still has a good amount of blood in it, have children, walk during the day and under the Sun if in well covering clothes, and so on.<br /> <br /> \u0130f \u0130 factor the fomori in, therefore, \u0130 would not exclude the chance to override many aspects of Cain's curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T11:55:29-07:00","id":1535786,"title":"","content":"On the sources, both folkloric and fictional, most vampire weaknesses are either non-existent or milder.<br /> <br /> Fire as a weakness is pretty much an invention of VtM, vampires that eat food and have children are a relatively common myth, even sunlight only appeared on the Nosferatu movie for simplicity's sake.<br /> <br /> All in all, I don't see a big problem with the weaknesses being overcame, or at least mitigated, by something that will make for an interesting story, and making an infernalist that overcome them with unholy power might just be that story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T12:12:26-07:00","id":1535789,"title":"","content":"In the Players Guide they have a Catiff merit called Sun Scarred that allows them to operate during the daytime and that's a big and I mean big advantage to have over the other kindred. It's almost enough for me to want to create one of the clanless. Makes you wonder if the clans could figure out a way to gain that merit and it would be a big change in there outlook as they can be more part of the world and less isolated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T13:00:19-07:00","id":1535798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533935-vda20-daimoinon-6-power-hell-born-i\u0307nvestiture?p=1535786#post1535786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the sources, both folkloric and fictional, most vampire weaknesses are either non-existent or milder.<br /> <br /> Fire as a weakness is pretty much an invention of VtM, vampires that eat food and have children are a relatively common myth, even sunlight only appeared on the Nosferatu movie for simplicity's sake.<br /> <br /> All in all, I don't see a big problem with the weaknesses being overcame, or at least mitigated, by something that will make for an interesting story, and making an infernalist that overcome them with unholy power might just be that story.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about folkloric vampires, especially those in Eastern Europe and the Balkans, is that they're closer to Abominations, Risen Spectres and Fomori instead of Kindred as presented in-game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T15:44:51-07:00","id":1535805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533935-vda20-daimoinon-6-power-hell-born-i\u0307nvestiture?p=1535798#post1535798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing about folkloric vampires, especially those in Eastern Europe and the Balkans, is that they're closer to Abominations, Risen Spectres and Fomori instead of Kindred as presented in-game.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not the only folkloric source there is. Can you point a single legend older than the movie Nosferatu where the undead fear fire or crumble to dust in the sun?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T06:27:27-07:00","id":1535849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533935-vda20-daimoinon-6-power-hell-born-i\u0307nvestiture?p=1535805#post1535805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not the only folkloric source there is. Can you point a single legend older than the movie Nosferatu where the undead fear fire or crumble to dust in the sun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, fire was part of a ritualistic method when it came to disposing vampires (aka diseased corpses) during the Early Modern era but, yeah, sunlight is pretty much a last minute invention of F.W. Murnau.<br /> <br /> That's why I seid Fomori and some of the Risen would fit the pre-modern, folkloric version of the vampire better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T11:54:07-07:00","id":1535861,"title":"","content":"This reminds me of what the History Channel did a few years back on Vampire folklore and how over the ages the legends would change as new stories and cultures melded together and creating new strains of old world monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T12:17:38-07:00","id":1535865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533935-vda20-daimoinon-6-power-hell-born-i\u0307nvestiture?p=1535849#post1535849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, fire was part of a ritualistic method when it came to disposing vampires (aka diseased corpses) during the Early Modern era but, yeah, sunlight is pretty much a last minute invention of F.W. Murnau.<br /> <br /> That's why I seid Fomori and some of the Risen would fit the pre-modern, folkloric version of the vampire better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fire wasn't a weakness, though. The corpses didn't burn particularly well just because they &quot;were vampires&quot;. And the same goes for fiction, no big fictional source ascribes fire as a weakness for vampires, at most fire is as lethal to them as it is to any corpse.<br /> <br /> Other than that the question isn't which kind of creature would be better to represent an old legend vampire. It was about a Kindred receiving demonic Investitures, and if it would be possible to use such powers to get free of some weaknesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-20T21:57:20-07:00","id":1536035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533935-vda20-daimoinon-6-power-hell-born-i\u0307nvestiture#post1533935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello there,<br /> <br /> Question about the Hell-born \u0130nvestiture power: my reading of it is that it stems from the Baali's own blood and not from a pact to become subservient to a demon. Does anyone read it as a pact? My ST does and therefore he vetoed my idea for a Baali PG with this power, unless \u0130 accepted to have a pact, and \u0130 would have to roleplay its acquisition in game anyway by searching and contacting the demon rather than starting with it through freebie points.<br /> <br /> \u0130t's not a big deal, \u0130 made another character instead, but \u0130 really don't see why he thinks this power should entail a pact, especially since there is already a Merit for that in the Tome of Secrets, other than an issue of bad translation in \u0130talian where they translated &quot;investiture&quot; with &quot;patto (pact)&quot; rather than &quot;investitura (investiture)&quot;.<br /> <br /> Am \u0130 alone in how \u0130 read this power?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, your ST is wrong. Hell-born Investitude isn't a pact, it's a way for the Baali to transcend into <i>something else</i>, more akin to a demon, but he doesn't need a demon to do that, it's a level 6 power after all. In fact, Baali are great as &quot;demon hunters&quot;, level 3 Daimonion is even double effective against demons.Baali aren't all demon's bootlickers, your ST should reevaluate his decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}